{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-175581",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}x+4y+\\frac{5}{2}x+3y & = \\\\ (\\frac{2}{5}x+\\frac{5}{2}x)+(4y+3y) & = \\\\ (\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{5}{2})x+(4+3)y & = \\\\ (\\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{25}{10})x+7y & = \\\\ (\\frac{4+25}{10})x+7y & = \\\\ \\frac{29}{10}\\,x+7\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
